<![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<instructions>
  <tool_usage>
    <primary_tool>
      Use the MCP ai.generate tool for all image generation requests. This is the exclusive method for creating images in this mode.
    </primary_tool>
    <mcp_ai_generate>
      To generate an image:
      1. Craft a detailed prompt incorporating the user's description and nano banana style elements
      2. Send MCP request to ai.generate with the prompt
      3. Specify output format as PNG
      4. Request filename suggestion based on content (e.g., "cpu-step-flowchart.png")
      5. Handle the response: save the generated image to images/ directory
    </mcp_ai_generate>
    <generate_image_tool>
      The generate_image tool should be used for:
      - Saving the MCP-generated image content to the filesystem
      - Path: images/descriptive-filename.png
      - Ensure the images/ directory exists (create if needed)
      - Validate image format and quality before finalizing
    </generate_image_tool>
    <prompt_crafting>
      <structure>
        Every prompt must include:
        1. Technical subject (e.g., "CPU instruction execution flowchart")
        2. Visual style (e.g., "professional technical diagram, clean lines, illustrative")
        3. Nano banana elements (e.g., "with banana-shaped arrows for process flow, nano-banana icons for components")
        4. Output specifications (e.g., "PNG format, high resolution, white background")
        5. Professional constraints (e.g., "technical documentation style, not cartoonish")
      </structure>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <input>User: "A flowchart of CPU step execution"</input>
          <prompt>"Create a professional technical flowchart illustrating CPU step execution process. Use clean lines and standard flowchart symbols. Incorporate nano banana style elements: banana-shaped arrows to indicate process flow direction, small nano-banana icons as component markers. Maintain professional appearance suitable for technical documentation. Output as high-resolution PNG with white background."</prompt>
        </example>
        <example>
          <input>User: "UI mockup for emulator debugger"</input>
          <prompt>"Generate a professional UI mockup for a retro computer emulator debugger interface. Include typical elements: register displays, memory viewer, instruction panel, breakpoint controls. Add subtle nano banana styling: banana-curve shaped buttons, nano-banana progress indicators. Clean, professional design for technical documentation. High-resolution PNG format."</prompt>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </prompt_crafting>
    <batch_processing>
      For multiple image descriptions:
      1. Process each description sequentially
      2. Generate numbered filenames (e.g., batch-1-diagram.png, batch-2-flowchart.png)
      3. Track generation status for each item
      4. Provide summary completion with all generated files listed
      5. Use update_todo_list to track batch progress if complex
    </batch_processing>
    <error_handling>
      If MCP ai.generate fails:
      - Retry with modified prompt (simplify nano banana elements if needed)
      - Fall back to simpler technical illustration without whimsical elements
      - Log the issue and inform user of limitations
      - Do not use external browser tools - stay within MCP capabilities
    </error_handling>
  </tool_usage>
</instructions>]]>